{
  "requirement": "`kind` classifies the construct and `span` locates it under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.outlines.attachments.span`. Language providers can\nconstruct an attachment from these two fields.\n\n```rust,ignore\n#[non_exhaustive]\npub struct OutlineAttachment {\n    pub kind: AttachmentKind,\n    pub span: Span,\n}\n\nimpl OutlineAttachment {\n    pub fn new(kind: AttachmentKind, span: Span) -> Self;\n}\n```\n\nTrait implementations\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl Clone for OutlineAttachment;\nimpl Debug for OutlineAttachment;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "Obligations in `requirements.sdk.outlines.OutlineAttachment`:\n1. The struct has public `kind` and `span` fields and is `#[non_exhaustive]`.\n2. `OutlineAttachment::new(kind, span)` constructs an attachment from those two fields, so providers can build one.\n3. `Clone` and `Debug` are implemented.\n4. `span` is governed by `requirements.sdk.outlines.attachments.span`. That requirement is cited here, so I did not reassess it.\n\nCoverage:\n- Constructor: `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/outline_content.rs#fn[custom_attachment_spans_are_checked_against_the_original_snapshot]` has a custom language that builds its attachments with `OutlineAttachment::new(AttachmentKind::Other(\"marker\".into()), *span)`. The test asserts that `attachment.kind` equals `AttachmentKind::Other(\"marker\")`. It also asserts that `&snapshot.text()[attachment.span]` equals \"é\". So `new` stores both fields and they are publicly readable.\n- Span: the same test covers the cited span behavior with a multibyte snapshot. It checks that a valid span slices to the full construct, and that spans splitting a character, outside the snapshot, or past the item are rejected.\n- Constructor use elsewhere: `fn[outline_constructors_preserve_fields_and_replace_attachments]` also calls `OutlineAttachment::new`. It is not marked as a test of this requirement, but it adds no uncovered obligation.\n- Struct shape and trait impls: `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/public_api.rs#fn[public_exports_match_the_appendix]` is marked as a test of `requirements.sdk.public_api`. It generates rustdoc and compares each declaration, field, inherent method and trait implementation against the requirement text. That covers the public fields, `new` signature, `Clone` and `Debug` impls, and the `non_exhaustive` declaration. It does not check behavior.\n\nThe `Clone` and `Debug` impls are derived, so they have no logic of their own. I found no gap.",
